From 9cf6032f21da336db10d651f4c9654d1e4b3d437 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 07:14:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] Warn and guide recovery before supporting skill
 files hit size cap

Supporting reference writes could grow silently to the 100k cap; refusal then
recommended splitting SKILL.md rather than the actual reference. The earlier
SKILL.md pressure fix excluded file_path patches and write_file operations.
Tests covered rejection but not reference warning or actionable recovery.

Apply label-aware pressure warnings on every growing supporting-file write,
include section sizes and ordered split/shrink/retry advice in cap errors.
Retain the cap, atomic rollback, and user-owned content movement. Structured
files explicitly require syntax/caller preservation instead of prose pointers.

Proof: three new regression cases failed before the fix. Focused size and
manager suites pass 114 tests; adjacent importer suites pass (390 tests in
initial run, with an extra out-of-scope binary-input test removed because
_guarded_write already rejects that input). Five source mutations killed,
covering recipe selection, both warning call sites, prior-size comparison,
and path-resolution refusal. scripts/check --base origin/main passes.
Recovery test preserves source and rolls back preceding batch writes on
failure, then preserves relocated text through split/shrink/retry.
